 (`0`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`) — `verts[0]` is read **unconditionally** before the loop, then the `for` never executes | returns `0` | `err_support_nonpositive_count` |\n| 13 | `c2Support` | `d == c2V(0,0)` → every dot is `0`, `dot > dmax` is never true | returns `0` (first vertex) | `err_support_zero_direction` |\n| 14 | `c2Support` | any `c2Dot(verts[i], d)` is `NaN` → `dot > dmax` false | that index is never selected | `err_support_nan` |\n| 15 | `c2Div` | `b == 0.0f` → `1.0f/0.0f = +inf` | `c2V(a.x*inf, a.y*inf)`: `±inf` for non-zero components, `NaN` for `±0.0` components | `err_div_by_zero` |\n| 16 | `c2Div` | `b == -0.0f` → `-inf` | `∓inf` / `NaN` | `err_div_by_zero` |\n| 17 | `c2Norm` | `a == c2V(0,0)` → `c2Len(a)==0` → `c2Div(a, 0)` | `c2V(NaN, NaN)` | `err_norm_zero_vector` |\n| 18 | `c2Norm` | `a` has an infinite component → `c2Len(a)==inf`, `1/inf==0` | `inf*0 = NaN` for that component | `err_norm_inf_vector` |\n| 19 | `c2Len` | `c2Dot(a,a)` overflows to `+inf` (e.g. `x = FLT_MAX`) | `sqrtf(inf) = inf` | `err_len_overflow` |\n| 20 | `c2Len` | any component is `NaN` | `sqrtf(NaN) = NaN` (no `errno`, no trap) | `err_len_nan` |\n| 21 | `c2GJK` | `ax_ptr == NULL` | `ax = c2xIdentity()` is used instead of dereferencing | `err_gjk_null_transforms` |\n| 22 | `c2GJK` | `bx_ptr == NULL` | `bx = c2xIdentity()` | `err_gjk_null_transforms` |\n| 23 | `c2GJK` | `outA == NULL` | the witness point A is simply not written; return value unaffected | `err_gjk_null_outputs` |\n| 24 | `c2GJK` | `outB == NULL` | witness point B not written | `err_gjk_null_outputs` |\n| 25 | `c2GJK` | `iterations == NULL` | iteration count not written | `err_gjk_null_outputs` |\n| 26 | `c2GJK` | `cache == NULL` | neither the cache-read block nor the cache-write block executes | `err_gjk_null_outputs` |\n| 27 | `c2GJK` | `cache != NULL` but `cache->count == 0` → `cache_was_good == 0` | cache is ignored, simplex is seeded fresh from vertex 0; cache is still **written** on exit | `err_gjk_cache_count_ze