en though the subtraction produced a non-zero value | `err_gjk_radius_shrink_collapse` |\n| 39 | `c2GJK` | `use_radius != 0` and `c2Sub(b,a)` is the zero vector inside the accepted branch | `c2Norm` of zero → `NaN` propagates into `outA`/`outB` | `err_gjk_radius_shrink_collapse` |\n| 40 | `c2GJK` | `typeA`/`typeB` not in `{0,1,2}` → `c2MakeProxy` leaves the **stack-local** `c2Proxy` uninitialised | **undefined behaviour** in C (reads indeterminate stack); not assertable byte-for-byte. Documented, and asserted only to be *non-crashing* + Rust-deterministic | `err_gjk_invalid_type_documented` |\n| 41 | `c2GJK` | `cache->count > 3` or `< 0` | **undefined behaviour**: writes past `c2Simplex.d` / reads `cache->iA[3]` (== `iB[0]`). Documented, not assertable | `err_gjk_invalid_type_documented` (doc-only) |\n| 42 | `c2GJK` | `cache->iA[i]`/`iB[i]` outside `[0, proxy.count)` | **undefined behaviour**: reads indeterminate `c2Proxy.verts[]` slots. Documented, not assertable | `err_gjk_invalid_type_documented` (doc-only) |\n| 43 | `c2Collided` | `typeA == C2_TYPE_CIRCLE`, `typeB` ∉ `{0,1,2}` → inner `default:` (lib.c:586) | returns `0` | `err_collided_invalid_enum` |\n| 44 | `c2Collided` | `typeA == C2_TYPE_AABB`, `typeB` ∉ `{0,1,2}` → inner `default:` (lib.c:598) | returns `0` | `err_collided_invalid_enum` |\n| 45 | `c2Collided` | `typeA == C2_TYPE_CAPSULE`, `typeB` ∉ `{0,1,2}` → inner `default:` (lib.c:610) | returns `0` | `err_collided_invalid_enum` |\n| 46 | `c2Collided` | `typeA` ∉ `{0,1,2}` → outer `default:` (lib.c:614); `B`/`typeB` never inspected | returns `0` (safe even with `A == NULL`) | `err_collided_invalid_enum` |\n| 47 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | `B.max.x < A.min.x` (`d0`) | returns `0` | `err_aabb_reject_axes` |\n| 48 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | `A.max.x < B.min.x` (`d1`) | returns `0` | `err_aabb_reject_axes` |\n| 49 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | `B.max.y < A.min.y` (`d2`) | returns `0` | `err_aabb_reject_axes` |\n| 50 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | `A.max.y < B.min.y` (`d3`) | returns `0` | `err_aa